  "body": "Found while working #882 (held branch `issue/882-adaptive-open-simplify` @ 70ac996f; see https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/882#issuecomment-6811353217).\n\n**What happens:** in motion `rotary_adaptive`, which developed levels are refused flips under every small change to the ring opening. In one variant, the level at radius 5.6 was cut by Offset rings **without a note naming the fallback**.\n\n**Why it matters:** \"Log diagnostics, never silence\". A planner that changes strategy for a level must say so in the operation's notes. A silent fallback hides why the toolpath differs from what the user chose.\n\nDone means: every adaptive level that falls back to rings carries a note naming the level and the reason, pinned by a test that forces the fallback on a rotary-developed level. The rotary_adaptive pins state which levels are refused for a reason that survives a sub-micron geometry change.\n\nPart of #882.\n",
